@{
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
    ViewBag.Title = "Part11 - Auto resize";
}

<div class="col-sm-12">
    <p>To make Fanex Grid auto re-size column, we do some steps below:</p>
    <p><b>Step 1</b>: Specific property <b>"autoResizeColumn"</b> with "true" in your grid options.</p>
    <p><b>Step 2</b>: Specific which column you will allow it auto re-size by adding <b>"CanResize"</b> property to column. If you have this property and also have <b>"Width"</b> property, for each column, grid will calculate max width of body and footer column, and compare to <b>"Width"</b> property, if it is greater than <b>"Width"</b> property, then grid will set it to <b>"Width"</b> property, or vice versa.</p>
    <p><b>Note</b></p>
    <p>For easy configuration, by default, grid will auto calculate how many pixel per character depend on font size. If you don’t wanna do that, you can override this by add <b>"pixelsPerCharacter"</b> to grid options, and value is how many pixel per character you want. This is apply for all column, you also can customize for each column by add <b>"PixelsPerCharacter"</b> to column property you want.</p>
    <p>For customize cell render, we can override <b>"CalResizeFunction"</b> function in column property, this function has input is column value, and output is how many pixel for this value.</p>
    <p><b>Below is example that we want grid:</b>
    <ul>
        <li>
            In first column, we want to customize calculation for re-size this column by estimation each character pixels
        </li>
        <li>
            In fourth column, we want to override "PixelsPerCharacter" for this column to 25
        </li>
        <li>
            Also for sixth column, with "PixelsPerCharacter" is 7
        </li>
        <li>
            And default we let grid auto calculate width by font size.
        </li>
    </ul>
    </p>
    <pre class="brush: javascript">
        var gridOptions =
        {
            columns: [
                { HeaderText: "Header 1", Width: 70, Name: "No", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "center", CanResize: true,
                    CalResizeFunction: function (value) {
                        return value.toString().length * 20;
                    }
                },
                { HeaderText: "Header 2", Width: 10, Name: "Text1", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "right", CanResize: true },
                { HeaderText: "Header 3", Width: 10, Name: "Number1", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "right", CanResize: true },
                { HeaderText: "Header 4", Width: 70, Name: "Number2", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "right", CanResize: true, PixelsPerCharacter: 25 },
                { HeaderText: "Header 5", Width: 70, Name: "Number3", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "right", CanResize: true },
                { HeaderText: "Header 6", Width: 10, Name: "Text2", CanResize: true, PixelsPerCharacter: 7 },
                { HeaderText: "Header 7", Width: 10, Name: "Text3", CanResize: true },
                { HeaderText: "Header 8", Width: 70, Name: "Text4", CanResize: true },
                { HeaderText: "Header 9", Width: 70, Name: "Number4", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "right", CanResize: true },
                { HeaderText: "Header 10", Width: 10, Name: "Number5", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "right", CanResize: true }
            ],
            bodyRows: bodyRows,
            gridExpandHeight: 150,
            numberOfFrozenColumn: 3,
            //autoFixFrozenRowHeight: true,
            autoResizeColumn: true,
            showPager: true,
            pagerOption: {
                itemsPerPage: 100,
                currentPage: 0,
                itemsPerPageArray: [50, 100, 500],
                showDetail: true
            },
            showFooter: true,
            footerRows: footerRows
            //,pixelesPerCharacter: 7.8
        };
        </pre>
    </div>
